I implemented `encode` and `decode` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`. I haven't run or tested anything, since shell access wasn't available.

`encode` finds each maximal run of a character. A run of 4 or more becomes `~n~c`. A shorter run is written out as itself, except that each `~` is doubled to `~~`.

`decode` reads left to right. It treats `~~` as one `~` and `~n~c` as `c` repeated `n` times. It accepts only ASCII digits in the count. It raises `ValueError` in each case the spec lists:
- a `~` at the end of the text;
- a `~` followed by something other than `~` or a digit;
- a count with leading zeros;
- a count below 4;
- a count not followed by `~`;
- a missing character after the second `~`.

